<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chen Yu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 204 BCE</span> · Also known as Chen Yu (Qin dynasty)</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chen Yu was a general of the revived state of Zhao during the rebellion against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin dynasty</a> and a sworn friend, later bitter enemy, of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhang-er">Zhang Er</a>. Passed over by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiang-yu">Xiang Yu</a> in 206 BCE, he drove Zhang Er from Changshan, restored <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhao-xie">Zhao Xie</a> and took the Kingdom of Dai. He was killed when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-xin">Han Xin</a> routed his army at Jingxing in 204 BCE.</p></div>
